      "note": "REFRESHED 2026-08-12 after the prior entry was found 12 days stale against its own 7-day TTL and missing 10 of 28 held names. The staleness was not cosmetic: the cached benchmark_return_1m_pct read -17.84% (30 Jun -> 30 Jul window, spanning the 07-28 crash) while the true trailing month is +0.73% -- an 18.6pp error that made almost every holding look like it was 'beating' a collapsing benchmark, so names_stretched collapsed to 2 names and the profit-take trigger had nothing to fire on. SKHY omitted: its ADR history starts after the anchor date, so a comparable 1m return does not exist -- nulled, never estimated. | 2026-08-12 intraday: added STM/TXN/AMD/COHR against the same 07-21 anchor and the same benchmark_return_1m_pct, so they are directly comparable to the existing 27. SKHY still omitted -- its ADR history starts after the anchor."
