        "text": "The 800G->1.6T transition is barely started and is supply-constrained at the laser, not at the module. Both LITE and COHR are shipping 1.6T today and COHR calls its ramp faster than it expected three months ago; NVDA is investing directly into laser/photonics capacity rather than module capacity. That is an early-innings, capacity-led upcycle, and it is a different clock from memory contract pricing, which is late in the HBM3E basis. The 2026-09-14 drawdown in this cluster was a financing-structure scare (GLW ATM) plus the Amodei pacing-essay sentiment shock, both of which the catalyst desk has since WEAKENED to unresolved-but-unescalated and sentiment-only respectively; Friday 09-18 (COHR +5%, LITE +3%, GLW +3%) recovered part of it against an unchanged order book.",
        "falsifier": "A hyperscaler or NVDA disclosing a 1.6T module order cut or a laser-capacity build pause; OR LITE/COHR reporting 200G/lane EML lead times SHORTENING materially into the Nov-2026 prints, which would say the binding constraint has cleared and the pricing power with it."
