        "text": "Downgraded from strengthening (09-09) to intact. Demand evidence is unchanged -- all three members raised FY26 guidance this summer (GEV 09-14, BE third raise to $3.9-4.2B, VRT raised EPS mid to ~$6.70) -- but two new facts show backlog is not near-term margin: GLJ's vintage math says GEV's 2027 deliveries carry ~3pp backlog margin vs 10-11pp on the 2028 vintage, and VRT missed Q2 revenue by ~$110M on supply-chain/execution timing, not orders. Monday's -7.5% cluster move was mostly factor (AI-slowdown essay + 10Y +32bps/1m), not demand: VRT -7.7% and BE -6.8% fell almost as much as GEV -8.6% with no vintage exposure. Mid innings: turbine price resets monetize in 2028, not 2027.",
        "falsifier": "GEV Q3 (2026-10-28) shows gas-turbine slot reservations or electrification orders down QoQ, OR VRT Q3 (2026-10-21) book-to-bill <1.0, OR a top-4 hyperscaler cuts 2027 capex guidance before 2026-11-15."
